<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Summa is distributed via Developer ID (not the Mac App Store), so the
	  App Sandbox is not required. We intentionally do not opt in because the
	  app needs:
	    - ScreenCaptureKit access to arbitrary on-screen windows
	    - User-chosen export folders preserved across launches (outside a container)
	    - Writes to ~/Library/Application Support/Summa for the training log

	  Hardened runtime is enabled at the build-settings level
	  (ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME=YES). We request no hardened-runtime exceptions:
	  no JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no DYLD environment variables,
	  no disable-library-validation. If we ever need one, add it here with a
	  comment explaining why.
	-->

	<!-- Sign in with Apple is intentionally NOT enabled. The App ID
	     (com.josephruocco.Summa) has the capability, the code is written, and a
	     Developer ID profile exists -- but Developer ID (outside-the-Mac-App-
	     Store) provisioning profiles do not carry the com.apple.developer.applesignin
	     entitlement, so the native flow can't be signed for this distribution
	     method. Revisit if/when distributing via the Mac App Store, or switch to
	     a web-based (ASWebAuthenticationSession) Apple OAuth flow. Until then the
	     beta access code is the sign-in. -->
</dict>
</plist>
